      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The scene continues, and a lawmaker named Senator Harris stands, his face a mask of indignation. \"Dr. Vasquez, your plan is nothing more than a way to turn citizens into pampered, useless dependents who have lost their purpose in life. The dignity of work is a fundamental human value. By stripping people of their jobs, you're stripping them of their dignity.\"\n\nDr. Vasquez's eyes never waver, her voice steady and clinical. \"Senator, your attachment to the 'dignity of work' is a psychological trap. In an age where AI can perform the majority of labor, tying human worth to work is not only cruel but also irrational. It's a relic of a primitive social contract that no longer exists. We are not pampered dependents; we are citizens in a post-labor economy. The old system is broken, and we must adapt or face extinction.\"\n\nShe steps closer to the podium, her presence commanding. \"The 'dignity of work' argument is a cruel illusion. It's a way to justify inequality and cling to a ghost of a past that no longer serves us. We must look forward, not backward. Universal Survival Dividend isn't about creating useless dependents; it's about ensuring",
